    title: "英國小型發電設施遭網路攻擊停擺四日，NCSC提醒關鍵基礎設施提升資安防護",
    summary: "英國一座小型燃氣尖峰發電設施於今年7月遭受網路攻擊，導致設施停擺了四天。雖然英國政府確認此事件影響僅限於小型能源發電設施，並未危及整體能源系統，但事件仍引起高度關注。根據報導，攻擊者身分疑似與伊朗相關駭客有關，但英國國家網路安全中心（NCSC）和政府尚未正式公布攻擊歸因或技術細節。NCSC此前已多次呼籲各組織，特別是關鍵基礎設施業者，應重新檢視資安防護措施，預先準備應對嚴重網路威脅。業界應提高警覺，加強能源系統的網路安全監控與應變能力，以應對來自國家級駭客的潛在威脅。",
    tags: ["英國", "NCSC", "能源基礎設施", "網路攻擊", "伊朗", "關鍵基礎設施"],
    title_en: "UK Small Power Facility Shut Down for Four Days Following Cyberattack; NCSC Urges Enhanced Cybersecurity for Critical Infrastructure",
    summary_en: "A small gas peaking power facility in the UK was hit by a cyberattack in July of this year, resulting in a four-day shutdown. Although the UK government confirmed that the incident was limited to the small energy generation facility and did not threaten the overall energy system, the event has drawn significant attention. Reports suggest the attackers may be linked to Iran-related hackers, but the UK's National Cyber Security Centre (NCSC) and the government have not yet officially released attribution or technical details. The NCSC has previously called on various organizations, especially critical infrastructure operators, to re-evaluate their cybersecurity defenses and prepare for severe cyber threats. The industry is urged to raise awareness, strengthen network security monitoring, and improve incident response capabilities for the energy system to counter potential threats from state-level hackers.",
    tags_en: ["UK", "NCSC", "Energy Infrastructure", "Cyberattack", "Iran", "Critical Infrastructure"],
    sources: [
      { name: "iThome", url: "https://ithome.com.tw/news/178462", lang: "ZH-TW" }
    ]
