    title: "親俄駭客群聲稱攻擊挪威公共數位服務，目標可能是削弱對烏克蘭的支持",
    summary: "挪威數位化機構（Digdir）的發言人透露，自上週一開始，該機構的數位服務持續遭受一次大規模的網路攻擊。此次攻擊被描述為「有史以來最大規模的攻擊」，駭客透過發動阻斷服務（DDoS）攻擊，向該機構推送大量流量，意圖癱瘓包括讓公民在多個公共服務中使用單一登入系統等關鍵服務。儘管遭受攻擊，Digdir仍表示服務「幾乎一直保持運作」。\n\n此次攻擊後，一個親俄駭客群體「Server Killers」在 Telegram 上聲稱了攻擊的責任，並宣稱這是因為挪威於 8 月 23 日恢復了與烏克蘭的安全合作，因此發動了網路戰。挪威總理 Jonas Gahr Støre 此前宣布，挪威將為烏克蘭提供為期三年的財政支持。\n\n歐洲各國自俄羅斯於 2022 年 2 月全面入侵烏克蘭以來，一直處於高度戒備狀態。官方指出，這些攻擊的目的是削弱歐洲社會對烏克蘭的支持，散播恐懼和不和，並耗費調查資源。此外，文章提及挪威過去曾遭受的、疑似與俄羅斯駭客相關的工業設施攻擊，包括控制水壩閥門的數位系統。",
    tags: ["挪威", "Digdir", "Server Killers", "DDoS", "網路攻擊", "烏克蘭", "國家資安"],
    title_en: "Pro-Russia Hacker Group Claims Attack on Norwegian Public Digital Services, Aiming to Undermine Support for Ukraine",
    summary_en: "A spokesperson for the Norwegian Digital Directorate (Digdir) revealed that since last Monday, the agency's digital services have been subjected to a large-scale cyberattack. The attack was described as the \"largest attack ever,\" with hackers pushing massive amounts of traffic via a Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS) attack, intending to paralyze critical services, including the single sign-on system used by citizens for multiple public services. Despite the attack, Digdir stated that services \"have remained operational almost continuously.\" Following the attack, a pro-Russia hacker group called \"Server Killers\" claimed responsibility on Telegram, stating that the cyberwarfare was launched because Norway resumed security cooperation with Ukraine on August 23. Norwegian Prime Minister Jonas Gahr Støre had previously announced that Norway would provide three years of financial support to Ukraine. Since Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine in February 2022, European countries have remained on high alert. Officials point out that the goal of these attacks is to undermine European society's support for Ukraine, spread fear and discord, and consume investigative resources. Furthermore, the article mentions past suspected attacks on Norwegian industrial facilities, potentially linked to Russian hackers, including digital systems controlling dam valves.",
