    title: "英國推動《網路安全與韌性法案》：擴大國家安全管制至核心基礎設施供應鏈",
    summary: "英國政府正在推動《網路安全與韌性法案》修正案，旨在建立更強大的國家安全防禦機制。此法案擴大了管制範圍，從過去僅限於通訊網路，延伸至管理型服務提供商（MSP）、資料中心、能源、水務、交通和醫療等所有核心基礎設施。根據新法，各部會部長可立即下令，要求相關機構停止採購、限制使用有風險的供應商產品或服務，甚至強制移除已安裝的設備。政府可將被制裁的設施名稱公佈，但會以國家安全為由，對具體風險供應商的名稱和詳細原因保密。此外，執行制裁的機構和諮詢方必須遵守保密規定。此舉旨在提前阻止與敵對國家相關的供應商，在發生實體網路攻擊或系統破壞之前，便能秘密地將其從國家關鍵供應鏈中移除，大幅提升國家基礎設施的韌性。",
    tags: ["英國政府", "Cyber Security and Resilience Bill", "國家安全", "核心基礎設施", "供應鏈風險", "GCHQ"],
    title_en: "UK Pushes Cyber Security and Resilience Bill: Expanding National Security Controls to Core Infrastructure Supply Chains",
    summary_en: "The UK government is advancing amendments to the Cyber Security and Resilience Bill, aiming to establish a more robust national security defense mechanism. This bill expands the scope of regulation, extending it from previously limiting communication networks to encompass all core infrastructure, including Managed Service Providers (MSPs), data centers, energy, water, transport, and healthcare. Under the new law, relevant ministers can immediately order organizations to cease purchasing, restrict the use of high-risk supplier products or services, or even mandate the removal of installed equipment. The government can publish the names of sanctioned facilities, but will maintain national security secrecy regarding the specific names and detailed reasons for the high-risk suppliers. Furthermore, organizations and consultants enforcing these sanctions must adhere to confidentiality regulations. This measure aims to preemptively remove suppliers linked to adversarial nations from the national critical supply chain, even before a physical cyber attack or system disruption occurs, thereby significantly enhancing the resilience of national infrastructure.",
