    summary_en: "A cybersecurity organization has issued a warning that multiple lines of Mitsubishi Electric FA products, including CC-Link IE TSN, MELSEC iQ-R, and MELSEC iQ-F, are generally affected by the CVE-2025-3511 vulnerability. This vulnerability allows remote attackers to cause a Denial of Service (DoS) state, timeout error, or communication delay on the target device by sending specially crafted UDP packets. The scope of affected products is extremely broad, covering various I/O modules, communication LSIs, and various CPU modules. Users are advised to immediately check their product versions and upgrade to a patched version as soon as possible to prevent operational disruption in critical infrastructure. Since the original text did not provide specific patched versions, users should refer to official Mitsubishi Electric announcements and take appropriate mitigation measures.",
