    summary_en: "Apple announced via the developer blog that it will update taxes and prices for App Store applications, In-App Purchases, and subscription services in multiple regions. The first round of changes took effect today, involving the introduction of a 20% VAT in Morocco and an 18% VAT in the Republic of the Congo, and an increase in the digital sales tax (DST) rate in Tanzania from 2% to 3%. The second round of price adjustments will begin on September 14th, affecting four countries: Israel, Indonesia, Morocco, and the Republic of the Congo. These price updates take into account the aforementioned tax rate changes. Developers should note that if any affected country is set as the base storefront for an application or In-App Purchase, that store's price will not change; however, prices in other stores will be adjusted to maintain balance with the base price. Apple emphasized that subscription services with automatic renewal, and stores where developers manually manage prices, will not be affected. Apple stated that these adjustments are a routine process for handling changes in tax regulations and foreign exchange rates.",
