    id: "20260827-114",
    trackers: ["os", "security"],
    category: "重點關注",
    title: "WhatsApp 整合 Passkeys 提升登入安全性：採用公私鑰加密取代傳統密碼與 OTP",
    summary: "全球最大的通訊平台 WhatsApp 宣布整合 Passkeys 功能，大幅提升用戶帳號的登入安全性。Passkeys 利用公私鑰加密技術取代傳統的密碼和一次性密碼 (OTP) 驗證，提供更快速、更不易被網路釣魚攻擊的登入體驗。此功能讓用戶只需透過生物識別或螢幕鎖定進行單點擊驗證，極大地減少了用戶操作的摩擦力。實務上，這不僅提升了登入速度，更重要的是，它提供了比傳統 SMS OTP 更可靠的保護機制，特別是在接收 SMS 服務不穩定的地區。對於開發者而言，WhatsApp 透過 Credential Manager API 實現了這一整合，確保了多樣化且穩健的帳號存取方式，避免用戶因單一存取方式失效而被鎖定。建議用戶和開發者應關注平台方提供的 API 介面，以確保應用程式能順利支援 Passkeys 的多重認證機制。",
    tags: ["WhatsApp", "Passkeys", "公私鑰加密", "OAuth", "資安", "多因素驗證"],
    title_en: "WhatsApp Integrates Passkeys to Enhance Login Security: Adopting Public-Private Key Encryption to Replace Passwords and OTP",
    summary_en: "WhatsApp, the world's largest communication platform, has announced the integration of Passkeys, significantly enhancing user account login security. Passkeys utilize public-private key encryption technology to replace traditional passwords and One-Time Passcode (OTP) verification, offering a faster and more resistant login experience against phishing attacks. This feature allows users to complete verification with a single tap using biometrics or screen lock, greatly reducing user friction. Practically, this not only speeds up the login process but, more importantly, provides a more reliable protection mechanism than traditional SMS OTP, especially in regions where SMS services are unstable. For developers, WhatsApp implemented this integration via the Credential Manager API, ensuring diverse and robust account access methods and preventing users from being locked out due to the failure of a single access method. Users and developers are advised to monitor the platform-provided API interfaces to ensure applications can smoothly support the multi-factor authentication mechanism of Passkeys.",
    tags_en: ["WhatsApp", "Passkeys", "Public-Private Key Encryption", "OAuth", "Cybersecurity", "Multi-Factor Authentication"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Android Developers Blog", url: "https://android-developers.googleblog.com/2026/08/whatsapp-passkeys-secure-sign-in.html", lang: "EN" }
    ]
