    id: "20260827-118",
    trackers: ["os"],
    category: "重點關注",
    title: "科技產業憂心：特朗普可能宣布新半導體關稅，恐衝擊AI發展與美國經濟",
    summary: "科技產業對美國可能實施的廣泛半導體關稅深感憂慮。根據 Politico 的報導，這些關稅可能在未來幾週或幾個月內實施，預計將對美國人工智慧（AI）的創新發展造成嚴重衝擊。消息人士指出，關稅框架可能會擴大，不僅針對晶片本身，甚至可能涵蓋使用晶片的下游產品，例如遊戲主機或資料中心伺服器，甚至可能課徵二手或翻新產品。Computer and Communications Industry Association (CCIA) 估計，此類關稅每年可能導致美國 GDP 損失約 900 億美元，並可能使 2030 年前規劃的資料中心專案中約 20% 延期或取消。CCIA 警告，這不僅會擾亂資料中心發展的動能，還可能導致更多資料中心開發外移，與特朗普旨在將發展帶回美國的目標背道而馳。產業呼籲政府考慮豁免某些產品，以避免造成廣泛的經濟漣漪效應。",
    tags: ["半導體", "關稅", "AI", "Donald Trump", "CCIA", "資料中心"],
    title_en: "Tech Industry Concerns: Trump May Announce New Semiconductor Tariffs, Threatening AI Development and US Economy",
    summary_en: "The tech industry is deeply concerned about potential broad semiconductor tariffs from the United States. According to Politico, these tariffs could be implemented within weeks or months and are expected to severely impact the innovative development of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in the US. Sources indicate that the tariff framework may expand, potentially covering not just the chips themselves, but also downstream products that utilize them, such as gaming consoles or data center servers. Tariffs might even be imposed on used or refurbished products. The Computer and Communications Industry Association (CCIA) estimates that such tariffs could cost the US economy approximately $90 billion in annual GDP loss and could lead to the delay or cancellation of about 20% of data center projects planned before 2030. CCIA warns that this would not only disrupt the momentum of data center development but could also cause more data center development to move abroad, contradicting Trump's goal of bringing development back to the US. The industry is calling on the government to consider exemptions for certain products to avoid widespread economic ripple effects.",
    tags_en: ["semiconductors", "tariffs", "AI", "Donald Trump", "CCIA", "data centers"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Ars Technica", url: "https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2026/08/ai-industry-says-trump-plans-to-tax-chips-in-the-single-dumbest-way-imaginable", lang: "EN" }
    ]
